      "en": "$bch_amt1"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "The flat monthly Child Benefit amount paid per qualifying child (€140/month in the current 2025-2026 system, per bch.md and the benefits description doc), payable for children under 16, or under 19 if in full-time education/training or unable to support themselves due to disability. In bch_ie's BenCalc it is assigned via Comp_perElig (\"monthly payment\"), so it is added once for every eligible child rather than once per family. Its latest raw formula, \"140#m*$sw_weeks\", multiplies the flat rate by $sw_weeks - a separate spine-wide bonus-scaling constant (labelled \"Xmas & Other Bonus\", valued 54/52 in 2025) - which folds extra one-off cost-of-living top-up payments into the modelled monthly figure; a Child-Benefit-specific version of the same mechanism was used in 2022-2024. It has been re-valued repeatedly since the model's first (2006) system year, ranging historically between roughly €130 and €166 before settling at €140."
    },
